{"availability":"available","full":"eai-support/eai","name":"eai","description":"Enterprise AI CLI for scaffolding, configuring, and operating EAI vertical applications.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":2,"created":"2026-03-08T23:49:44Z","updated":"2026-10-12T01:40:58Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://eai-support.github.io/eai/","topics":["ai","cli","developer-tools","docusaurus","enterprise-ai","github-pages","gofer","typescript"],"demo":"https://eai-support.github.io/eai/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T02:04:56.644Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T02:04:56.644Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T02:04:56.644Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T02:04:56.644Z","stars":1,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Scaffold, configure, validate, and operate EAI applications from a developer terminal.","The CLI gives teams a supported path for application setup, authentication, workspace selection, runtime validation, resource management, and deployment readiness. It keeps platform access behind authenticated commands and public-safe diagnostics, so developers and AI coding agents get useful next steps without exposing private infrastructure details.","Customer-facing CLI language uses workspace. The CLI also accepts the tenant command and --tenant- options for compatibility with existing scripts and platform API names. Stable fields such as tenantId, --tenant-id, limits.tenants, and role IDs such as tenant-admin remain unchanged. They refer to EAI workspaces or the platform role contract."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eai-support/eai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b7e2180ae5c072b00933e7225707c932e44449ce47f14e21b3812a0e7fd7e736","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T02:04:56.773Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T02:04:56.773Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Scaffold, configure, validate, and operate EAI applications from a developer terminal.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eai-support/eai/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"eai login --callback-port still uses for the OAuth callback; it just pins the port instead of choosing a random one.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eai-support/eai/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"It still uses your current login and workspace context, and PublicAPI still enforces platform workspace authorization.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eai-support/eai/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"b7e2180ae5c072b00933e7225707c932e44449ce47f14e21b3812a0e7fd7e736","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eai-support/eai/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T02:04:56.773Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-12T01:40:58Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/eai-support/eai/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T02:04:56.776Z","hash":"b7e2180ae5c072b00933e7225707c932e44449ce47f14e21b3812a0e7fd7e736","originalBytes":41605,"storedBytes":41605,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T02:04:56.644Z","subjects":[],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"Developer tools","subjects":[],"evidence":[],"platformEvidence":[],"platformSupport":"author_metadata_not_runtime_tested","suggestedSubjects":["Automation & workflows","MCP servers & agents","Templates & UI components"],"reviewRequired":true},"demoHealth":{"url":"https://eai-support.github.io/eai/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-12T02:17:45.289Z","probeVersion":3,"status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T02:17:45.289Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-12T02:17:45.289Z","target":"https://eai-support.github.io/eai/","failureCount":0,"consecutiveTemporaryFailures":0,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-19T02:17:45.289Z"},"previewAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T02:17:45.289Z","previewCheck":{"url":"https://eai-support.github.io/eai/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-12T02:17: